The shm is allocated before checking `iov_iter_npages()`. When `iov_iter_npages()` returns 0 (e.g., due to a zero-length input), the error path jumps to `err_ctx_put`, which only releases the context reference but does not free the previously allocated `shm`, causing a memory leak.

